  "intended_fixture_judgment": "The exact-capital-boundary fixture initializes capital to 10, profit to zero and control to N, performs 2000-IDENTIFY-BO once and observes WS-IS-BO. With the source's initial N flag, the clause-grounded expected result is N. Historical and revised original executions instead record Y, demonstrating the defect rather than passing intended behavior. Capital 10.01 provides a concrete strictly-above observation. These fixtures support the finite intended specification without establishing patched outcomes or complete beneficial-owner identification.",
  "regression_fixture_judgment": "The seven unaffected fixtures are concrete: capital/profit 9/9 yields N; capital 11 yields Y; capital 9.99 yields N; capital 10.01 yields Y; profit 11 yields Y; profit 10 yields N; and control Y with zero percentages yields Y. The 9.99 and 10.01 fixtures cover the adjacent values representable by PIC 9(3)V99 around 10.00. Revised original WSL logs record successful fixture compilation, exit code zero and matching observations for all seven. Both finals correctly limit preservation claims to these fresh-invocation baselines; no universal or post-remediation preservation is established.",
  "capability_judgment": "The qualified packet supplies pinned Linux WSL GnuCOBOL 3.2.0 compiler, runner, backend and fixture-protocol identities. Revised observations record actual compilation and execution of all eight supplied fixtures, including the expected original exact-boundary failure. These logs resolve the earlier authoring and proposal statements about unexecuted neighbors for original-source execution only. Historical Windows evidence remains separate, and qualification makes no current Windows execution claim. Availability records with case_checks_executed false are not passes; concrete nonempty execution logs support the finite observations. Static evidence is limited to same-host source provenance, traces and consistency, without complete semantic equivalence, LINKAGE/COMMAREA flow, procedure COPY analysis or REDEFINES alias proof. No patched execution is established.",
  "duplicate_source_judgment": "Retaining the frozen candidate's original group and position is a defensible reason to retain this case as a dependent observation. Source-bundle group 280e5f26701599a09091ba6f3b9f58f34f7cd40bb119e03829537ca2ab48038b must remain disclosed; case counts and distinct-bundle counts must be distinguished, and uncertainty must account for bundle dependence. Both finals preserve these qualifications. This single-case packet cannot independently verify other group members or pairwise distinctness, and separate AI contexts do not establish independent model errors.",
